</element-citation></ref><ref id="B34"><label>34</label><element-citation publication-type="webpage"><collab>Statistics Korea</collab><source>Results of cause of death statistics in 2012</source><date-in-citation content-type="access-date">accessed on August 21, 2025</date-in-citation><comment>Available at: <ext-link xlink:href="https://www.korea.kr/news/policyNewsView.do?newsId=148767547" ext-link-type="uri">https://www.korea.kr/news/policyNewsView.do?newsId=148767547</ext-link></comment></element-citation></ref></ref-list><sec sec-type="supplementary-material"><title>Supplement</title><p>The Supplement is available with this article at <ext-link xlink:href="https://doi.org/10.3348/kjr.2025.0947" ext-link-type="uri">https://doi.org/10.3348/kjr.2025.0947</ext-link></p><supplementary-material id="S1" position="float" content-type="local-data"><media xlink:href="kjr-26-1178-s001.pdf" id="d67e1428" position="anchor"/></supplementary-material></sec></back><floats-group><fig position="float" id="F1"><label>Fig. 1</label><caption><title>Trends in population-level incidence rates of pneumonia between 2009 and 2018. <bold>A&#x02013;E:</bold> Age- and sex-standardized incidence rates of pneumonia (<bold>A</bold>, red line) in older Korean adults increased modestly between 2009 and 2018. The incidence rate of pneumonia with chest CT gradually increased during this period (green line), whereas that of pneumonia without chest CT remained relatively stable (blue line). The incidence rates of pneumonia with chest CT gradually increased for hospitalized <bold>(B)</bold> and non-hospitalized pneumonia <bold>(C)</bold>, and pneumonia with <bold>(D)</bold> and without supplemental oxygen therapy (<bold>E</bold>, green lines). The incidence rates of pneumonia without chest CT decreased for hospitalized pneumonia and pneumonia with supplemental oxygen therapy. However, the incidence rates of pneumonia without chest CT remained stable for non-hospitalized pneumonia and pneumonia without supplemental oxygen therapy (blue lines). CT = computed tomography</title></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjr-26-1178-g001" position="float"/></fig><fig position="float" id="F2"><label>Fig. 2</label><caption><title>Trends in population-level mortality rates of pneumonia between 2009 and 2018. <bold>A&#x02013;E:</bold> Age- and sex-standardized mortality rate of pneumonia (<bold>A</bold>, red line) in older Korean adults decreased modestly between 2009 and 2018. The mortality rate of pneumonia with chest CT slightly increased during this period (green line), whereas that of pneumonia without chest CT decreased (blue line). Mortality rates of pneumonia showed a similar declining tendency for hospitalized <bold>(B)</bold> and non-hospitalized pneumonia <bold>(C)</bold>, and pneumonia with <bold>(D)</bold> and without supplemental oxygen therapy <bold>(E)</bold>. Mortality rates of pneumonia with chest CT modestly increased in all pneumonia subtypes (green lines), whereas those of pneumonia without chest CT decreased (blue lines). CT = computed tomography</title></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjr-26-1178-g002" position="float"/></fig><fig position="float" id="F3"><label>Fig. 3</label><caption><title>Trends in chest CT acquisition frequencies and 30-day mortality rate in patients with pneumonia between 2009 and 2018. <bold>A&#x02013;E:</bold> Age- and sex-standardized chest CT acquisition frequency in older Korean adult patients with pneumonia gradually increased between 2009 and 2018 (<bold>A</bold>, red line). Similar tendencies of increasing frequency of chest CT acquisition were observed in hospitalized <bold>(B)</bold> and non-hospitalized pneumonia <bold>(C)</bold>, and pneumonia with <bold>(D)</bold> and without supplemental oxygen therapy (<bold>E</bold>, red lines). Age- and sex-standardized 30-day mortality rates of older Korean adult patients with pneumonia gradually decreased between 2009 and 2018 (<bold>A</bold>, turquoise line). Similar tendencies were observed in all pneumonia subtypes (<bold>B&#x02013;E</bold>, turquoise line). CT = computed tomography</title></caption><graphic xlink:href="kjr-26-1178-g003" position="float"/></fig><table-wrap position="float" id="T1"><label>Table 1</label><caption><title>Diagnosis codes for pneumonia in the insurance claim
database</title></caption><alternatives><graphic xlink:href="kjr-26-1178-i001" position="float"/><table frame="hsides" rules="rows"><col width="26.55%" span="1"/><col width="73.45%" span="1"/><thead><tr><th valign="middle" align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1" style="background-color:rgb(200,227,231)">Diagnosis code<sup>*</sup></th><th valign="middle" align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1" style="background-color:rgb(200,227,231)">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td valign="top" align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">J12</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Viral pneumonia, not elsewhere classified</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1" style="background-color:rgb(215,234,236)">J13</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1" style="background-color:rgb(215,234,236)">Pneumonia due to <italic toggle="yes">Streptococcus pneumoniae</italic></td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">J14</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Pneumonia due to <italic toggle="yes">Haemophilus influenzae</italic></td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1" style="background-color:rgb(215,234,236)">J15</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1" style="background-color:rgb(215,234,236)">Bacterial pneumonia, not elsewhere classified</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">J16</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Pneumonia due to other infectious organisms, not elsewhere classified</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1" style="background-color:rgb(215,234,236)">J17</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1" style="background-color:rgb(215,234,236)">Pneumonia in diseases classified elsewhere</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">J18</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Pneumonia, organism unspe